 FFmpeg is licensed LGPL-2.1 or later, with parts of it under GPL-2 or later.
 This package is configured with --enable-gpl, which links those parts in,
 and with --enable-version3, which configure requires for rkmpp and rkrga:
 both are in its EXTERNAL_LIBRARY_VERSION3_LIST. That takes the whole to
 GPL-3 or later, which is a consequence of the hardware support this package
 exists for and not a choice that was open.
 .
 The full text of the GNU General Public License version 3 is in
 /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3 on a Debian system. The upstream source
 carries COPYING.GPLv2, COPYING.GPLv3, COPYING.LGPLv2.1, COPYING.LGPLv3 and
 the per-file headers that say which applies where.

